"A NumberToString is a <textTypeConverter> that transforms a numeric subject value to a <readableString> for use by its client. If the subject value is nil it is converted to an empty string and vice versa. When converting a client string back to a subject value the most appropriate class of Number is chosen to represent the value.

Instance Variables:
	format	<readableString> or nil, reserved for future use."

AbstractToTextConverter subclass: NumberToText [
    | _reserved1 |

    leftToRight: aNumber [
        "Answers the result of converting aNumber to a String"
        #todo.	"Numbers should be displayed through the Locale, but at present the rightToLeft operation is only implemented for Smalltalk format."
        	^aNumber displayString
    ]
    rightToLeft: aString [
        "Answers the result of converting aString to a Number."
        ^Number fromString: aString
    ]
]
